# Git — push when you work (mandatory)

GitHub (`origin/master`) is the source of truth. bkweb3 pulls CIS shell from here.

**Do not ask for permission** to commit and push after a code task — just do it.

## After every task that changes code

Before ending your turn:

1. `git status` — confirm you are in `Carbo-CIS`, not the parent folder.
2. Stage only intentional changes (explicit paths, not blind `git add .`).
3. Never commit secrets or local-only build artifacts unless explicitly requested.
4. One logical change per commit; concise message (why, not file list).
5. `git commit` then `git push origin master`.
6. Report commit hash in your summary.

If the user asked only a question (no edits), skip.

## Deploy path

Server: `/opt/carbo/carbo-cis` — `git pull` then `bash deploy_on_server.sh` or `sync_cis_shell_on_server.sh`.

## When push fails

Report the error; do not leave the user thinking work is on GitHub when it is not.
